Kruger National Park (KNP) is located in the northeastern part of South Africa, stretching along the border with Mozambique to the east, Zimbabwe to the north, and the Crocodile River to the south.
The public park has an area of 19,500 square meters and is divided into 14 distinct eco-friendly zones, each supporting different species of wild animals.
It is one of the most popular tourist destinations in South Africa and is also regarded as a significant site of South Africa's National Parks (SANParks).
The park collects daily maintenance fees and entrance fees, just like other national parks in South Africa.
In addition, it may also benefit those who purchase the Wild Card, which grants access to any national park of their choice in South Africa and all national parks throughout South Africa.
